³1ip³2205.231.146.31³2ts³21074332684³2version³21³2name³2text_default³2data³2summary³3answer Junker³3text³3= Bill St. Clair's Messages =

Leave questions and messages for me here. Maybe I'll even remember to check. Put new messages at the top, so we dont' have to scroll down.

----

:m040116a: fm Junker

:Odd this place-idea.  I've been thru Wikipedia before, and.... They've got a 'discuss page' for each page. Good idea, I'd say. Can you hook the option, or do you want us to link our own? <nowiki>PageName</nowiki> has, say, <nowiki>PageNameDiscussion</nowiki> or <nowiki>PageNameTalk</nowiki>, and so for any given page-name.

:Also, maybe I see amazon links to personal sections of amazon. seems who updates the page last will get their percentage. probly be a link war. thoughts?

040116: BillStClair

I see no way in the UseMod wiki code to automatically create a discussion link. I suppose I could figure out how to do it, but I'm no Perl fan. For now, create your own.

I noticed the amazon IDs as well, and wondered what to do about it. Seems to me that it's fair for the first person to link to a book to get the credit. If people want to start a link war, there's not much I can do about it. I don't want to engage in a ban war, either.

:m040117a: fm Junker

:Fine. 'Talk' is shorter than 'discussion', so I'll try it. I only recently installed Linux, so I am short on Perl. Are you willing to give advice on Linux-site creation-wiki installation or...? I have a hard time figuing out how to get the ISP servers to act. Seems I'm missing some basic ideas on how cgi relates things. Loaded scripts but all I could get was one error or the other. Not high priority. I go along as I can.

:Saw back-and-forth on Wikipedia on whose definition of what was to reign, seems it was ?anarchism?-left vs. right. I did not stay long enough to see how things were worked out, but it seems there is nothing to do but watch and see who tires out first or whether they come to a compromise solution.

:It seems to me that talk about design, goals, structure and such will help progress. Maybe the <nowiki>TitleTalk</nowiki> pages will fill that. We'll see. Thanks.

:BOY, am I slow. I just noticed the new icon. Brilliant. No vote needed.

040117: BillStClair

Why do you put m...a around the date? I'm accustomed to yymmdd dates. They're nice because they sort correctly alphabetically. And is "fm" short for "from". Probably extraneous.

I like your <nowiki>TitleTalk</nowiki> idea.

I'll put some wiki configuration advice at UseModSetup.

I'm not willing to call the new icon final yet. It's a nice idea, but the image itself is sort of monochrome and boring. I want to see Matt Apple's black and gold version, and maybe someone else will come up with something even more brilliant.
